mkdir makes the directory: yes
open makes the file: yes
write writes it: yes
close closes it: yes
O_EXCL refuses it again with EEXIST: yes
read reads it back: yes
lseek moves the offset: yes
read reads from the offset: yes
fstat answers a regular file and its size: yes
isatty answers no, with ENOTTY: yes
write to a file open to read is EBADF: yes
fopen appends: yes
stat answers the appended size: yes
symlink makes a link: yes
symlink refuses a name that exists with EEXIST: yes
readlink answers its target: yes
readlink of a file is EINVAL: yes
lstat answers the link: yes
stat follows it: yes
realpath resolves it: yes
chdir enters the directory: yes
rename renames by a relative path: yes
the old name is gone with ENOENT: yes
the listing has the file: yes
the listing has the link: yes
rmdir of a full directory is ENOTEMPTY: yes
chdir leaves it: yes
unlink removes the file and the link: yes
rmdir removes the directory: yes
it is gone with ENOENT: yes
